```
$ gen-circleci-orb generate -h
Generate orb source files from a CLI binary's --help output

Usage: gen-circleci-orb generate [OPTIONS]

Options:
  -h, --help  Print help (see more with '--help')

Source:
      --binary <BINARY>  Name of the binary to introspect (must be on PATH)
      --config <CONFIG>  Path to gen-circleci-orb.toml config file

Output:
      --output <OUTPUT>
          Project root directory (orb source is written to
          `<output>/<orb-dir>/`) [default: .]
      --orb-dir <ORB_DIR>
          Subdirectory within --output where orb source is written
      --orb-namespace <NAMESPACES>
          CircleCI orb namespace(s) to publish the orb under (repeatable)
      --home-url <HOME_URL>
          Home URL for the orb registry display section
      --source-url <SOURCE_URL>
          Source URL for the orb registry display section

Docker image:
      --install-method <INSTALL_METHOD>
          How the binary is installed in the generated Docker image
          [possible values: binstall, apt, local]
      --base-image <BASE_IMAGE>
          Base Docker image for the generated executor
      --circleci-cli-version <CIRCLECI_CLI_VERSION>
          circleci-cli version to install in the generated Docker image
          executor (overrides `[orb].circleci_cli_version` and the built-in
          default)
      --apt-packages <APT_PACKAGES>
          Extra apt package(s) to install in the final Docker image stage
          (repeatable)
      --cargo-tool <CARGO_TOOLS>
          Extra cargo tool(s) to install into the executor image
          (repeatable)

Behavior:
      --git-push-subcommand <GIT_PUSH_SUBCOMMANDS>
          Subcommand name(s) whose generated jobs should include a
          set_https_remote step (repeatable)
      --dry-run
          Show planned output without writing any files
      --no-record
          Suppress auto-record for this run, even when `[record].enabled =
          true` in gen-circleci-orb.toml
      --check
          Verify mode: regenerate the orb and compare it to the committed
          files, writing nothing and never recording
      --allow-main-record
          Allow auto-record to push to `main`

```
